er','labview','visa'))]\"","timeout":30000,"description":"List python/powershell processes at T0"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_011apFabpFKPnT5TqfxRmGb7","tool_input":{"command":"for f in \"C:/Program Files/National Instruments/LabVIEW 2026/user.lib/claudeDev/D1_s1_copy.vi\" \"../Min_Track N beads V6_ParallelLoop.vi\"; do echo \"== $f\"; grep -a -b -o \"Rotor\\|ASRL5::INSTR\\|'Rotor'\" \"$f\" | head; done","timeout":30000,"description":"Byte-scan S1 and its source for rotor resource strings"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01QdnHBgCU7Yn41EDPTEYM26","tool_input":{"command":"py -c \"import json;d=json.load(open('tools/bench/decisions_pending.json',encoding='utf-8'));print({k:v for k,v in d.items() if k!='items'});it=d['items'];print(len(it));print(json.dumps(it[-1],ensure_ascii=False,indent=1))\"","timeout":30000,"description":"Show decisions_pending header and last item"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_018qSG9wqs8icKiZKxNX7yNB","tool_input":{"command":"py tools/bgrun.py --max-min 10 --log tools/bench/retro.log -- py tools/retrospective.py --cycle 104","timeout":600000,"description":"Run the cycle-104 retrospective under bgrun"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01W326cxMkjWdxkzo4JgQSRj","tool_input":{"command":"until tail -n +3468 tools/bench/retro.log | grep -qE \"BGRUN (END|TIMEOUT|KILLED)\"; do sleep 5; done; tail -n +3468 tools/bench/retro.log | grep -E \"BGRUN (END|TIMEOUT|KILLED)|^VIOLATION|archived as|^VERDICT\" | cut -c1-900","timeout":600000,"description":"Wait for the cycle-104 retrospective end line and show its verdict"}},{"tool_name":"Monitor","tool_use_id":"toolu_01P2dZALcmnoFewfFUrHLjzy","tool_input":{"description":"cycle-104 retrospective end","timeout_ms":600000,"command":"until tail -n +3468 tools/bench/retro.log | grep -qE \"BGRUN (END|TIMEOUT|KILLED)\"; do sleep 5; done; tail -n +3468 tools/bench/retro.log | grep -E \"BGRUN (END|TIMEOUT|KILLED)|^VIOLATION|archived as|^VERDICT\" | cut -c1-900"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":6,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":6,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":1,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":6,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{"material":6}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":82,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Cycle 104 is done. The display-loop VI is built and saved, but its frame-loss test (ABBA: legs A, B, B, A) produced no numbers. Every leg stopped about 4 s after Run, before bead picking. The unchanged copy of the original (S1) stops the same way, so the new VI is not the cause.\n\n**What was built:** `claudeDev\\D1_s1_disp_20260927_041648.vi`, md5 `245a1020…`. It passes all the structural checks, but it has never been run.\n- **Part B build:** it took three runs, all without saving anything over the original copy or the Part A file.\n  - Run 1 stopped at step 43 on a bug in our build script. It looked up a loop by its real ID in a table keyed by simulated IDs. Fixed; the script's self-test now catches it.\n  - Run 2 executed steps 34–47 with no differences, but the equivalence check (E3) found only 6 of the 21 expected changed connections.\n  - Run 3 passed every check and saved the file by script.\n- **Why only 6 of 21:** the other 15 expected rows came from how the simulator builds its graph (no labels, no flat-sequence tunnel pairs). They already appear on the unedited original, and each one is fed from the same source as in the original. So the real change is exactly the 6 intended connections plus 8 new objects. I rewrote the check that way (Pre-decided 217(c)), and the dry run now evaluates it too. Memory peaked at 613 MB, under the 700 MB stop.\n\n**Why the ABBA failed:**\n- In every leg the rotor setup subVI (`Configure.vi`, rotor on COM5) opened its window and the run ended.\n- The S1 copy ran normally on 09-26 at 14:18. COM5 was free before and after the run (not checked during it). No other program was holding it, and the cycle's motor setup never touched COM5.\n- A reviewer pointed out that no error dialog was seen, so \"automatic error handling stopped it\" is not yet shown.\n\n**Retrospective:** one fault, which I accept. The test driver ran legs 2–4 after the first leg had already failed on the known-good S1 file, costing 17 minutes and adding nothing. Leg drivers must now stop as soon as an S1 leg fails before bead picking.\n\n**Next cycle (105):** one diagnostic card.\n1. Read by script which serial port name S1 passes to the rotor setup subVI.\n2. Run one S1 leg that records every window's title and text every 0.5 s from Run onward, so any error message is captured before the harness closes it.\n\nThe ABBA reruns only after the cause is known, with its pass/fail rule unchanged (Pre-decided 217(f), fixed before any numbers existed). The tooling card follows.\n\n**Questions for you** (both in `tools/bench/decisions_pending.json`; neither stops the runner):\n- **D-2026-09-27-02 (new):** did anything change on the rig since 09-26 afternoon, such as rotor controller power, its USB cable, or a PC restart?\n- **D-2026-09-27-01 (still open):** whether to keep going with the display-loop work as planned. Cycles 102–104 went ahead on \"yes\".\n\nAlso: the Figma connector needs authorising in your claude.ai connector settings before it can be used.\n\n`tools/bench/next.json` and STATUS.md's `## NEXT` are written, and the retrospective review file has its notes filled in.","ttft_ms":2164,"type":"result","duration_ms":6941370,"uuid":"f58ccc21-ed0d-4f64-b8bc-60d7ced3a7a9","ttft_stream_ms":2030,"time_to_request_ms":261,"first_content_frame_ms":2030,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
